From: CarPlay C0 lane (2026-11-22)
Subject: 0526 sweet_nub: only dereference ctl+0x110/0x120 when the value looks like a pointer

0525 is the first boot that built the device tree: after "registered as ncmBringup" the probe's
5 s sample printed child[0] IOUSBDeviceConfigurator, child[1] IOUSBDeviceInterface,
child[2] IOUSBDeviceInterface, children 3 -- the configurator matched and createUSBDevice made both
NCM interfaces. S0/S2/S3/S4/S5 were all True.

Then the probe killed itself: the 0519 diagnostic printed "ctl+0x110 = 0x5ac00000000..." and
dereferenced it as an object pointer, so the kernel took a data abort at 15.195 s (pc
0xfffffff0079ef73c). ctl+0x110 legitimately holds a packed value at this point, not a pointer.

0526 only dereferences values that could be a kernel object address (>= 0xfffffff000000000 and
8-byte aligned) and prints ", not a pointer" otherwise, so the census stays readable without taking
the machine down.

Device evidence: outputs/data-a-live-nezha/device/private/logs/1795313400 (the crash follows the
children 3 line, 1 ms after ctl+0x110 was printed).

--- a/libkern/c++/sweet_nub.cpp
+++ b/libkern/c++/sweet_nub.cpp
@@ -512,12 +512,23 @@
 	 */
 	for (unsigned off = 0x110; off <= 0x120; off += 0x10) {
 		void *obj = *(void **)((char *)ctl + off);
+		uint64_t raw = (uint64_t)obj;
 		printf("SWEET NUB: ctl+0x%x = %p", off, obj);
-		if (obj != NULL) {
+		/*
+		 * 0526: on the 0525 boot this loop crashed the kernel at 15.195 s, right after the 5 s
+		 * sample had already shown child[0] IOUSBDeviceConfigurator and two IOUSBDeviceInterface
+		 * children. ctl+0x110 held 0x5ac00000000..., i.e. a packed value, not a pointer -- the
+		 * old code dereferenced it unconditionally. Only follow values that could actually be a
+		 * kernel object address, and say so when the field is something else: the 18-slot / tag
+		 * census can then be read from the log instead of from a panic.
+		 */
+		if (raw >= SWEET_NUB_KERNEL_BASE && (raw & 7) == 0) {
 			void **vt = *(void ***)obj;
 			if (vt != NULL && (uint64_t)vt >= SWEET_NUB_KERNEL_BASE) {
 				printf(", vtable %p, slot29 %p", vt, vt[29]);
 			}
+		} else if (raw != 0) {
+			printf(", not a pointer");
 		}
 		printf("\n");
 	}
